  "body": "### What is the issue with the XMLHttpRequest Standard?\n\nIn synchronous [send()](https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#the-send()-method), step 12.6 terminates the fetch on timeout, and step 12.7 unconditionally reports timing.\n\n  Fetch’s [report timing](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#finalize-and-report-timing) starts with:\n\n  > Assert: controller’s report timing steps is non-null.\n\n  Those steps are initialized by processResponseEndOfBody in [fetch response handover](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-finale). A sync XHR in a worker can time out before that initialization, tripping the assertion.\n\n  Should timing reporting be skipped in this case, or should Fetch initialize the reporting steps on termination?",
